102	/**
103	 * A client that consumes records from a Kafka cluster using the {@link GroupProtocol#CLASSIC classic group protocol}.
104	 * In this implementation, all network I/O happens in the thread of the application making the call.
105	 *
106	 * <p/>
107	 *
108	 * This {@link ConsumerDelegate} implementation exists for backward compatibility to allow users to continue to use
109	 * the classic group protocol (pre-KIP 848).
110	 *
111	 * <p/>
112	 *
113	 * <em>Note:</em> This class should not be invoked directly; users should instead create and use the
114	 * {@link KafkaConsumer} API as before.
115	 */
